---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cycle Easy - Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Cycle Easy - your privacy-first period tracker. We collect nothing. Your data stays on your device."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/cycle-easy/privacy"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] mb-12">Cycle Easy - Period Tracker &middot; Effective February 15, 2026</p>

        <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          
          <div class="privacy-highlight">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">🔒 The Bottom Line</h2>
            <p class="text-lg"><strong>Cycle Easy collects absolutely nothing.</strong> Your period data, symptoms, and cycle history never leave your device. There are no servers. There is no cloud. There is no way for us — or anyone else — to access your information. Ever.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Why This Matters</h2>
            <p class="mb-3">We built Cycle Easy because we believe menstrual health data deserves the strongest possible privacy protections. In today's world, this data is uniquely sensitive. We refuse to create any system that could potentially be compelled to reveal your private health information.</p>
            <p><strong>We can't share what we don't have.</strong> This isn't a policy choice — it's an architectural one. There is literally no mechanism for your data to leave your device through our app.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Data Storage</h2>
            <p>All data — your period dates, symptoms, predictions, and settings — is stored locally on your device using Apple's SwiftData framework. This data is:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Stored only on your device</strong> — nowhere else</li>
              <li><strong>Protected by your device passcode</strong> and Face ID/Touch ID</li>
              <li><strong>Encrypted by iOS</strong> using your device's security</li>
              <li><strong>Never transmitted</strong> to any server, ever</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">No Accounts</h2>
            <p>There is no sign-up, no login, no user account. You download the app and start using it immediately. We have no way to identify you, track you, or associate any data with you.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">No Cloud Sync</h2>
            <p>Your data does not sync to iCloud, our servers, or any third-party service. If you delete the app, your data is permanently erased. If you get a new phone, you start fresh (unless you restore from an encrypted device backup you control).</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">No Analytics or Tracking</h2>
            <p>Cycle Easy contains:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>No analytics frameworks</strong> (no Firebase, Mixpanel, Amplitude, etc.)</li>
              <li><strong>No crash reporting services</strong> (no Sentry, Crashlytics, etc.)</li>
              <li><strong>No advertising SDKs</strong></li>
              <li><strong>No tracking pixels</strong></li>
              <li><strong>No third-party code</strong> that could collect data</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3">We don't know how many people use the app. We don't know what features are popular. We accept this trade-off because your privacy matters more than our analytics.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">No Network Requests</h2>
            <p>Cycle Easy makes zero network connections. The app works entirely offline. You could use it in airplane mode forever. The only network activity associated with the app is through the App Store for initial download and updates — both handled by Apple, not us.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Apple HealthKit (Optional)</h2>
            <p class="mb-3">Cycle Easy can optionally write menstrual cycle data to Apple Health. This feature is:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Disabled by default</strong> — you must explicitly enable it</li>
              <li><strong>Controlled entirely by you</strong> — you choose what to share</li>
              <li><strong>Local to your device</strong> — governed by Apple's privacy policy</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3">If you enable HealthKit sync, data flows only between Cycle Easy and Apple Health on your device. We never see this data. Cycle Easy only writes to HealthKit; it does not read any health data from other sources.</p>
            <p class="mt-3">You can disable HealthKit at any time in the app settings. Data already written to Apple Health remains there (managed by Apple Health, not us).</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Your Control</h2>
            <p>You have complete control over your data:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Export</strong> — Download all your data as a JSON file anytime</li>
              <li><strong>Delete</strong> — Erase all data with a single tap</li>
              <li><strong>Uninstall</strong> — Removing the app permanently deletes all data</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>Cycle Easy does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children under 13. Since we collect no data from any user, there is no children's data to protect.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Legal Requests</h2>
            <p>We cannot comply with legal requests for user data because we possess no user data. There are no servers to subpoena, no databases to search, no records to produce. Your data exists only on your device, protected by your device's security and any legal protections that apply to your personal property.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>If this policy changes, we will update this page with a new effective date. However, our core commitment will never change: <strong>Cycle Easy will never collect, store, or transmit your personal data.</strong> Any app update that changed this would be a completely different app.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Contact</h2>
            <p>Questions about our privacy practices? Email us at <a href="mailto:privacy@idlefusion.com" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">privacy@idlefusion.com</a>.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-highlight {
    background: rgba(225, 29, 72, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(225, 29, 72, 0.15);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  :global(.dark) .privacy-highlight {
    background: rgba(251, 113, 133, 0.08);
    border-color: rgba(251, 113, 133, 0.2);
  }

  .privacy-highlight p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
